course: dictionary
lesson: 14485
title: Pathway: a route to follow
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A pathway is a path or track that people walk along, often through a garden, park or field. «The pathway wound through the park to the duck pond.» Look at the two parts of the word, path and way. A pathway is a way along a path.
explain: The word can also mean a route to a goal. «Hard work is the pathway to becoming a vet.» Nobody is walking here. A pathway is the way you travel towards something you want, such as a job or a level at school.
explain: In science, a pathway is a route that something follows through the body or brain. «Signals travel along nerve pathways to your fingers.» Check the clues around the word to see which meaning fits.
fact: A pathway is a path or track, often through a garden, park or field.
fact: A pathway can also be a route to a goal, such as a career.
fact: In science, a pathway is a route that something follows, like nerve pathways in the brain.
fact: «Stay on the pathway» near cliffs or water keeps you safe.
fact: Pathway is a noun: one pathway, two pathways.
exercise: «The little pathway led past the roses to the gate.» What is the pathway here? | *A path that people walk along | A kind of cloud | A loud noise | A bird that sings
exercise: «Her pathway to becoming a doctor began with volunteering.» What does pathway mean here? | A type of sports shoe | A bridge over a river | *A route to reach a goal | A hole in the ground
exercise: «Nerve pathways carry signals to your brain.» What does nerve pathways mean? | Tiny stones in the road | Sleeping places for nerves | *Routes that signals follow | Heavy rocks
test: «Stay on the pathway near the cliff edge.» Why is this good advice? | Pathways are always wet | *It keeps you safe from falling | It is quicker to run | It makes the cliff taller
test: «The cycle pathway runs beside the river.» Where would a cyclist ride? | *A track for bikes beside the river | A road for cars only | Inside the water | Across the sky
exam: «The science lesson explained the pathway food takes through the body.» What does pathway mean here? | *A route that something follows | A sports game | A garden path | A school subject
